![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `safeReadJson` function parses JSON directly using `JSON.parse` without a `try-catch` block. If the target file is malformed, this will throw an unhandled exception and crash the script. Wrapping it in a `try-catch` block ensures that malformed critical artifacts are handled gracefully, allowing the script to fail-closed as required by the general rules.

```javascript
function safeReadJson(filePath) {
  if (!fs.existsSync(filePath)) {
    return null;
  }
  try {
    const raw = fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8');
    return JSON.parse(raw);
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
```

